  ],
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\group.inverse:of{x}:in{G ::= (X, *, e)}]\nDeclares: y \"in\" G\nwhen:\n. G is \\group\n. x \"in\" G\nexpresses:\n. x * y = e\n. y * x = e\nDocumented:\n. called: \"group inverse of $x?$\"\n. written: \"x+?^{-1}\"\n. description: \"The inverse $x^{-1}$ of an element $x$ of a group is the unique\n                element $y$ satisfying $x * y = e = y * x$. Its uniqueness is\n                proved below; it is what allows every equation in a group to be\n                solved.\"\nId: \"9b52b844-0cfa-4238-8c73-8b38265cca81\"",
